#! ia 1.0

@convention repo-package-kind-roles
  meaning
    says "Public dependency-role grammar for the seven optional package.kind values (omitting package.kind leaves a package unclassified). Each role is defined purely by dependency responsibility without fixed rank numbers: contract holds shared types, schemas, interfaces and protocol definitions with zero runtime I/O and depends only on contract packages; core holds deterministic domain or algorithmic logic free of host, transport and storage I/O and depends only on core or contract packages; adapter translates between contract/core abstractions and concrete external boundaries such as storage, network, filesystem or SDK clients; view renders user-interface components and state projections without becoming a deployable entrypoint; composition wires core, adapter and view packages for one application slice and never imports sibling composition packages at the same layer rank; host is a deployable runtime entrypoint (server, CLI, worker or desktop shell) that no other package imports; and tool is a build, codegen or verification utility that runtime packages never depend on. Reference: assets/repo-vocabulary.md."
    answers "What does each package.kind value mean in public dependency-role terms?"
  governance
    severity advisory
    requires "Classify package.kind by dependency role (contract, core, adapter, view, composition, host or tool) without tying the vocabulary to fixed rank numbers, or omit package.kind when unclassified."
  subject
    subject-word package

@convention repo-schema-vs-checker-standing
  meaning
    says "Distinguish what the IA 1.0 schema enforces at admission, what the offline check-layers verifier enforces mechanically, and what stays repository convention. Schema admission checks required fields, typed references, package.kind enum membership and @system relationship consent rows (including cite repository|layer|package|area using spec and area's three consent rows). check-layers enforces strictly decreasing layer.rank on @layer require edges, package.layer consistency with any @package require @layer edge, non-increasing layer.rank on @package require @package edges, cycle freedom across @layer, @package and @area require graphs, unique non-overlapping canonical package.path roots, non-empty area.packages, credential-free repository.url, and dependency-role purity on classified packages. Multi-area package membership, whether package.kind is mandatory for a repository, and whether an external build-policy file overrides descriptive records remain repository-level conventions. Reference: assets/repo-vocabulary.md."
    answers "Which repository rules are enforced by schema admission, which by check-layers, and which are conventions?"
  governance
    severity advisory
    requires "State schema-enforced, checker-enforced and convention-only standing explicitly rather than claiming the schema checks rank order, cycles or multi-area exclusivity."
  subject
    subject-word layer
